# WhitecardVision — JS code regions (ValeSpec style)

Applies to first-party modules under `WhitecardVision/`. **Exclude** anything under `WhitecardVision/00__ThirdParty__**/`, vendored bundles, and `node_modules`.

## Rules

1. **Regions use `//` line comments only** — do not use `/* REGION | … */` or `/* FUNCTION | … */` for structure.

2. **File-level wrapper** (immediately after the file header block):
   - Opening: three lines — `// =============================================================================`, `// REGION | <Short module title>`, `// =============================================================================` (use `=` rule lines, same as ValeSpec).
   - After the main IIFE / module body, before `window.…` assignments: `// endregion ===================================================================` (double `=` line matches file scope).

3. **Inner sections** (long files with distinct phases): use **narrow** rule lines, then `REGION |`, then the same rule line. Close with `// endregion -------------------------------------------------------------------` (dashes, same width as the opening `---` block). Match ValeSpec `DocumentModel`-style nesting.

4. **Function- and block-level** (all sizes): use `// SCOPE | Title` (e.g. `// FUNCTION |`, `// HELPER FUNCTION |`, `// PUBLIC API`, `// MODULE CONSTANTS |`) and short dividers:
   - `// ------------------------------------------------------------`  
   Place one before and one after each logical function or return block (ValeSpec `StateManager` / `DocumentModel` rhythm).

5. **Simpler modules** may use **only** file-level `// REGION` + function-level `// … |` blocks (no inner `// REGION` sections) when the file is a single concern.

6. **Do not** change runtime behavior in a “regions-only” pass — comments and blank-line layout only.

## Reference

Copy patterns from `WebApps/ValeSpec/02__Src__AppModules/`, e.g. `ValeSpec__AppCore__StateManager__.js` and `ValeSpec__DocPreview__DocumentModel__.js`.

## Anti-patterns

```javascript
/* REGION | … */
/* FUNCTION | … */
/* ------------------------------------------------------------ */
```

## Preferred

```javascript
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// REGION | Section Title
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

    // FUNCTION | DoSomething
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    function DoSomething() { }
    // ------------------------------------------------------------

// endregion -------------------------------------------------------------------
```
